---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import CtaBand from '../components/CtaBand.astro';

const faqs = [
  ['Is Jurnl cloud software?', "No. It's a desktop app. Your database is on your computer and is synced through a shared folder you choose, such as OneDrive. Jurnl itself never holds your data."],
  ['Do I need OneDrive or another cloud drive?', "No, not if you're the only person using it. Keep the company in a folder on your own computer; Jurnl encrypts it and makes backups. A cloud drive is only needed when other people work on the same company, and then everyone uses the same one. Jurnl also copies your backups to a second place, such as a USB drive, so a broken computer doesn't take your books with it."],
  ['Can more than one person use it?', 'Yes. Up to four people who edit and three read-only users, each with their own sign-in and role. One person edits at a time; Jurnl locks the shared copy while someone is working and tells others who has it.'],
  ['Can I share the books with someone who uses a different cloud drive?', "Not for working on them together. Everyone who works on a company must sync the same shared folder from the same provider, for example all on OneDrive or all on Dropbox. With OneDrive, outside people such as your accountant need a Microsoft 365 work account, either their own organisation's or one you add for them. For anyone else, make a read-only copy."],
  ['Can my accountant or lender look at my books without syncing my folder?', "Yes. Make a read-only copy for them: one encrypted file they open in Jurnl with their own password, free and with no cloud account. You choose whether it includes payroll and employee names, and personal and bank details are always left out. If they don't use Jurnl, email them the accountant pack (PDFs and an Excel workbook) instead."],
  ['Does it work offline?', "Yes. You work on a local copy; it's saved back to the shared folder when you're online again, and Jurnl warns you while you're offline."],
  ['Is my data secure?', 'The whole database is encrypted, and tax file numbers, dates of birth, addresses and bank details are encrypted a second time. Each person signs in with their own password, and every change is recorded in an audit trail.'],
  ['Does it do Single Touch Payroll?', 'Yes. Jurnl produces the Single Touch Lite file for each pay date and keeps the full STP Phase 2 breakdown. Lodging STP directly from Jurnl is in development.'],
  ['Which pay rules does it follow?', "The ATO's 2026–27 withholding schedules (including working holiday makers, no TFN, foreign residents and study loans), the superannuation guarantee on ordinary time earnings, and the ATO's rules for unused leave and employment termination payments."],
  ['Does it handle awards?', 'You set up the pay items you need (overtime rates, allowances, penalty-style loadings) and leave loading. Jurnl does not interpret modern awards for you.'],
  ['Can I do my BAS from it?', 'Yes. The activity statement gives G1, G2, G3, G10, G11, 1A, 1B, W1, W2 and PAYG instalments on cash or accrual basis, and the GST detail report shows every transaction behind each label. You lodge it with the ATO as usual.'],
  ['Which banks does it work with?', 'Any bank that exports statements as CSV or Excel and accepts ABA (direct entry) files for payments, which covers the major Australian banks. Direct bank feeds are in development.'],
  ["I'm not registered for GST. Can I use it?", 'Yes. Turn GST off for the company and invoices, bills and the activity statement leave GST out.'],
  ['Can I run more than one business?', 'Yes. Add as many companies as you like, each with its own folder, people and branding.'],
  ['What does my accountant get?', 'An accountant pack: profit and loss, balance sheet, trial balance, general ledger, GST and PAYG by quarter and a payroll summary, as PDFs and one Excel workbook, with employees shown by payroll ID only.'],
  ['Is there a free trial?', "Yes. Fill in the short form on the Free trial page and we'll email you a link to download Jurnl. It's free to use with one company and up to three current employees, and a free trial licence lifts the limits. During the trial, Single Touch Payroll is reported with the ATO's Single Touch Lite file; lodging directly from Jurnl comes once the ATO approves it. Opening a read-only copy never needs a licence."],
  ['What happens when Jurnl is updated?', "Jurnl updates itself on Windows and Mac: it looks for updates each time it starts and installs them when you close it. Before a new version changes anything, it backs up your database and keeps that backup, then shows you what's new. Updates work during the trial too."],
  ['Which computers does it run on?', 'Jurnl is a desktop app for Windows 10 or 11 (64-bit) and Macs with Apple silicon (M1 or later).'],
  ['Is it for Australian businesses only?', "Yes. Its tax tables, Single Touch Payroll, activity statement, bank files and ABN, TFN and BSB checks are all Australian."],
];
---

<BaseLayout title="FAQ" description="Straight answers about Jurnl: desktop, not cloud; working alone or with others; read-only copies; security; Single Touch Payroll; BAS; banks; GST; the free trial; updates." section="faq">
  <section class="page-hero">
    <div class="container stack" style="--gap: 18px">
      <h1 class="h1" style="font-size: clamp(2.125rem, 4.2vw, 3.25rem)">Straight answers</h1>
      <p class="lead muted">Questions people ask about Jurnl.</p>
    </div>
  </section>
  <section class="section">
    <div class="container" style="max-width: 900px">
      <div class="faq-list">
        {
          faqs.map(([q, a]) => (
            <details>
              <summary>{q}</summary>
              <p>{a}</p>
            </details>
          ))
        }
      </div>
      <p class="muted" style="margin-top: 32px">Something else? <a href="/contact/">Ask us</a>.</p>
    </div>
  </section>
  <CtaBand />
</BaseLayout>
